You are absolutely right! That is a brilliant architectural catch.
Because your React UI has a **"Step 3: Set Execution Preference"** screen, the batch is not *truly* submitted to the Checkers until the Maker clicks that final **"Submit"** button (which calls updateBatchSchedule).
If we send the notification during createBatchRequest (Step 2), the Checkers will get an alert while the Maker is still staring at the scheduling screen!
Here is exactly how to move the notification to trigger **only** when the schedule is finalized and the batch officially becomes Pending ('P').
### 1. Remove the Notification from createBatchRequest
In your VoucherCommandService.java, find the createBatchRequest method. Scroll to the bottom and **DELETE or COMMENT OUT** the notification line so it doesn't fire prematurely:
```java
        // ==========================================
        // SMART NOTIFICATION ROUTING
        // ==========================================
        // REMOVE THIS LINE:
        // notificationWriterService.createNextStepApprovalNotification(batchId, nextApproverRoleId, stageName);

        // ---> TRIGGER 1: LOCK THE VID AS USED <---
        if (dto.getVid() != null && !dto.getVid().isEmpty()) {
            workflowEngine.updateVidStatus(dto.getVid(), VoucherStatus.USED);
        }

```
### 2. Add the Notification to updateBatchSchedule
Now go to the updateBatchSchedule method in the same file. We will dynamically fetch the Stage Name and Role ID, and trigger the notification exactly when the batch flips to 'P' (Pending).
Update the bottom half of your updateBatchSchedule method to look exactly like this:
```java
        // SMART DOUBLE-LOCK LOGIC:
        // Check if the AsyncWorker is still writing data. (If actual rows match requested rows, it's done!)
        String checkDataLoadedSql = """
            SELECT CASE WHEN p.RECORDS_COUNT = (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM VOUCHER_POSTING_DATA d WHERE d.BATCH_ID = p.BATCH_ID) 
            THEN 1 ELSE 0 END FROM VOUCHER_POSTING p WHERE p.BATCH_ID = ?
        """;

        Integer isDataLoaded = jdbcTemplate.queryForObject(checkDataLoadedSql, Integer.class, batchId);

        if (isDataLoaded != null && isDataLoaded == 1) {
            // 1. Data is fully loaded. Safe to show to checkers!
            jdbcTemplate.update("UPDATE VOUCHER_POSTING SET BATCH_STATUS = 'P' WHERE BATCH_ID = ?", batchId);
            
            // 2. FETCH WORKFLOW DETAILS FOR NOTIFICATION
            try {
                String wfSql = """
                    SELECT wt.ALLOWED_ROLE_ID, wt.DESIGNATION 
                    FROM VOUCHER_POSTING vp 
                    JOIN WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS wt ON vp.WORKFLOW_CODE = wt.WORKFLOW_CODE 
                    WHERE vp.BATCH_ID = ? AND wt.WORKFLOW_ORDER = 2
                """;
                Map<String, Object> step2Info = jdbcTemplate.queryForMap(wfSql, batchId);
                
                String nextApproverRoleId = String.valueOf(step2Info.get("ALLOWED_ROLE_ID"));
                String stageName = (String) step2Info.get("DESIGNATION");
                
                // 3. SEND THE NOTIFICATION TO THE CHECKERS NOW
                notificationWriterService.createNextStepApprovalNotification(batchId, nextApproverRoleId, stageName);
                
            } catch (EmptyResultDataAccessException e) {
                log.error("Could not find Step 2 workflow configuration for Batch {} to send notification.", batchId);
            }

        } else {
            // Data is still inserting. Leave it as 'S'. 
            // (Make sure your AsyncWorker sends the notification when it finally flips the status to 'P'!)
            log.info("Schedule saved for Batch {}, but data is still loading. Status remains 'S'.", batchId);
        }
    }

```
### Why this is the perfect solution:
 1. **No False Alarms:** The Checkers will never receive an alert while the Maker is still deciding on the scheduled time.
 2. **Dynamic Stage Names:** It queries the database in real-time to get the exact DESIGNATION (e.g., "Level 1 Checker") so the text correctly says: *"Voucher Batch '0000930' has advanced to 'Level 1 Checker' and requires review."*
 3. **Data Safety:** It only sends the notification if isDataLoaded == 1. This prevents Checkers from clicking the notification link and seeing an empty batch because the Excel file is still uploading in the background!
